{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-040",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 40,
  "title": "Job 40",
  "display_title": "Job 40",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 40,
  "sortOrder": 18040,
  "verseCount": 24,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Moreover the LORD answered Job, and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Shall he that contendeth with the Almighty instruct him? he that reproveth God, let him answer it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Then Job answered the LORD, and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Behold, I am vile; what shall I answer thee? I will lay mine hand upon my mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Once have I spoken; but I will not answer: yea, twice; but I will proceed no further.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Then answered the LORD unto Job out of the whirlwind, and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Gird up thy loins now like a man: I will demand of thee, and declare thou unto me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Wilt thou also disannul my judgment? wilt thou condemn me, that thou mayest be righteous?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Hast thou an arm like God? or canst thou thunder with a voice like him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Deck thyself now with majesty and excellency; and array thyself with glory and beauty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Cast abroad the rage of thy wrath: and behold every one that is proud, and abase him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Look on every one that is proud, and bring him low; and tread down the wicked in their place.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Hide them in the dust together; and bind their faces in secret.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Then will I also confess unto thee that thine own right hand can save thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Behold now behemoth, which I made with thee; he eateth grass as an ox.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Lo now, his strength is in his loins, and his force is in the navel of his belly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "He moveth his tail like a cedar: the sinews of his stones are wrapped together.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "His bones are as strong pieces of brass; his bones are like bars of iron.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "He is the chief of the ways of God: he that made him can make his sword to approach unto him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Surely the mountains bring him forth food, where all the beasts of the field play.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "He lieth under the shady trees, in the covert of the reed, and fens.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "The shady trees cover him with their shadow; the willows of the brook compass him about.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Behold, he drinketh up a river, and hasteth not: he trusteth that he can draw up Jordan into his mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:40:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "He taketh it with his eyes: his nose pierceth through snares.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 40:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:40:24"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
